    "content": "John Ratcliffe is the Director of the Central Intelligence Agency (D/CIA), having been sworn in on January 23, 2025. He serves as the head of the CIA and reports to the Director of National Intelligence (DNI), managing intelligence collection, analysis, and operations. Key Details About Current Director John Ratcliffe: Background: Ratcliffe is an attorney and politician who previously served as the 6th Director of National Intelligence (2020–2021). Distinction: He is the first person to serve as both Director of National Intelligence and Director of the CIA. Previous Roles: Served as a U.S. Representative for Texas's 4th congressional district (2015–2020) and as U.S. Attorney for the Eastern District of Texas. Role Focus: Manages the CIA's efforts in intelligence collection, covert action, and counterintelligence. Key CIA Positions & History: Deputy Director (DD/CIA): Supports the Director in managing daily agency operations. Recent Directors: Preceded by William Burns (2021–2025) and Gina Haspel (2018–2021). Confirmation: The Director is nominated by the President and confirmed by the U.S. Senate. The Director of the CIA is responsible for ensuring the agency delivers actionable intelligence to the President and other decision-makers.",
